      "summary_md": "# Episode summary\n\nInstruction: pick up the alphabet soup and place it in the basket.\nResult: official success=false; server returned max_moves and terminated=true in its final result after 25 moves and 264 physics steps. The can visually rested inside the basket, but the official check did not confirm success. Do not count this as a successful trial.\n\nConfirmed +x toward bottom of agentview. Approached the front red/green soup can with open jaws. First close was too far behind the can: gripper_open fell from 0.138 to 0.026 during the test lift and the can stayed on the floor. Reopened and advanced in two 2cm commands. Second close at measured eef approximately (0.1404, 0.0257, 0.0637) retained opening 0.748; test lift and subsequent lifts moved the can with the gripper. Carried it left/back above basket, lowered, released, and retracted. All motions reported reached rather than blocked/contact. Too many small descent corrections consumed the planner budget, leaving no opportunity to adjust final placement or allow more settling. Exact reason the official placement predicate stayed false is unknown.\n\nHindsight: World +x moves toward BOTTOM of agentview; +y toward LEFT. Floor scene support approximately z=0, home measured z=0.2487. A lid centered in wrist image is insufficient: actual pad contact is near the bottom of wrist frame. Initial close at x=0.111, z=0.0534 missed behind can; forward correction to measured x about 0.140 and z about 0.064 produced a stable body grasp with gripper_open about 0.74. Small target commands commonly left 6–9mm residual, so repeated tiny descents were inefficient. Keep closed command explicit during transport. Lift to about z=0.21 before crossing basket rim. Release was near measured (0.008, 0.239, 0.162); visually inside basket but not officially successful. Reserve more planner calls for placement and settling.\n",
